  ["Isolating the aerosol signal from the much larger effect of changes in cloudiness (Harshvardhan, Ch. 3).", "Open; it is now the central methodological problem of the field under the names co-variability and confounding. Requiring N_d to mediate the AOD–cloud-fraction relationship removes about 80% of it; inverted-V LWP–N_d relationships are argued to be co-variability.", "Gryspeerdt et al. 2016, 2019; Goren et al. 2025; Arola et al. 2022"],
  ["A global inventory of the principal sources and nature of CCN is required (Hobbs, Ch. 2; Harshvardhan, Ch. 3).", "Partly resolved. Satellites give global AOD but AOD is a poor CCN proxy; in situ work finds sea spray supplies less than 30% of marine CCN over most of the globe, the remainder being mainly non-sea-salt sulfate entrained from the free troposphere; natural-aerosol uncertainty still dominates ERFaci uncertainty.", "Stier 2016; Quinn et al. 2017; Carslaw et al. 2013"],
  ["The role of organics in CCN formation is potentially important but has not been quantified (Hobbs, Ch. 2).", "Partly resolved. The single-parameter (κ) hygroscopicity framework quantifies organic CCN activity; ocean-derived organic enrichment of submicron marine particles has been measured; but organic fraction and mixing state remain leading sources of error in predicting CCN.", "Petters & Kreidenweis 2007; Russell et al. 2010; Riemer et al. 2019"],
  ["Do 'sulfate aerosols' exist in the strict sense, or are all aerosols mixed? (Jaenicke, Ch. 1)", "Open as a quantitative problem. Mixing state is now measurable at the single-particle level and is known to affect CCN activity, but integrating mixing-state measurements with models is identified as an outstanding challenge.", "Riemer et al. 2019"],
  ["Long time-series of CCN spectra at a variety of locations are needed; long aerosol records should serve understanding, not only monitoring (Hobbs, Ch. 2; Jaenicke, Ch. 1).", "Partly resolved. Multi-year CCN, size-distribution and composition records exist at 12 regionally representative observatories, and in situ optical-property records of 10–40 years at 52 stations; marine coverage is sparse and largely campaign-based (EPCAPE is one year).", "Schmale et al. 2018; Collaud Coen et al. 2020; Russell et al. 2025"],
