  ["Does DMS emission increase with temperature, and do DMS-derived particles reach CCN size? (the CLAW hypothesis; Hobbs, Ch. 2)", "Resolved in the negative. Two decades of observational, laboratory and modeling work led to the conclusion that biological control of CCN by DMS probably does not exist and that the hypothesis should be retired.", "Quinn & Bates 2011"],
  ["Anomalous absorption of solar radiation by clouds (King, Ch. 5).", "Largely resolved. After a renewed controversy in 1995, the dedicated ARM aircraft experiment ARESE II found measured absorption matched models to within about 10% on most days and did not support the large anomalies reported earlier.", "Cess et al. 1995; Pilewskie & Valero 1995; Ackerman et al. 2003"],
  ["Retrievals rest on Mie theory and plane-parallel transfer; horizontal inhomogeneity has not been explored (King, Ch. 5).", "Partly resolved. 3-D radiative transfer theory and tools are mature and 3-D effects are quantified in specific cases (surface irradiance enhancements above 150 W m⁻² in broken cumulus), but operational and ground-based retrievals still assume plane-parallel clouds, and heterogeneity bias remains a recognized limitation on N_d.", "Marshak & Davis 2005; Gristey et al. 2020; Grosvenor et al. 2018"],
